+
+### `createPatch(from, to)`
+
+Computes the [JSON Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6902) (RFC 6902) that turns `from` into
+`to` when applied with `applyPatch`, and returns it as a new array. Neither input is mutated.
+
+- `from`: any JSON-compatible value, the starting document.
+- `to`: any JSON-compatible value, the document to reach.
+
+The patch only covers what actually changed: unchanged object members and array elements are left
+out, and a change nested deep inside the document produces an operation scoped to that location rather
+than replacing an enclosing object or array wholesale. Array elements are matched by deep equality (via
+a longest-common-subsequence comparison), so inserting or removing an element in the middle of an array
+produces a single `add` or `remove` rather than a `replace` of every element shifted around it.
+
+Every pair of JSON-compatible values has such a patch, so, like `applyMergePatch`, this function never
+throws.
