@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+---
+id: task-005-implement-json-patch-diff-rfc-6902-createpatch
+type: task
+title: "Implement JSON Patch diff RFC 6902 createPatch"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Clients want to send only what changed between two versions of a JSON document instead of the whole
+new version. Add `createPatch(from, to)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, that returns an RFC 6902 JSON
+Patch turning `from` into `to` when applied with the existing `applyPatch`, without mutating either
+input, and describing only what changed.
+
+## What was done
+
+- Added `createPatch(from, to)` to `src/index.ts`, plus the private helpers `diffValues`,
+  `diffObjects`, `diffArrays`, and `escapeToken`.
+- Objects are diffed member by member (`add`/`remove`/recurse); arrays are diffed as a longest common
+  subsequence by deep equality, so a single middle insertion or removal costs one operation instead of
+  replacing every shifted element; any other change recurses or falls back to a single `replace`.
+  Design rationale recorded in dl-004.
+- Reused the existing `deepEqual` and `isJsonObject` helpers already used by `applyPatch` and
+  `applyMergePatch`, and added `escapeToken` (the encode-side counterpart of the existing
+  `unescapeToken`) to build correctly-escaped `~`/`/` paths for member names.
+- Documented `createPatch` in `README.md` alongside the other three exported functions.
+- Test-first: added failing tests to `src/index.test.ts` (covering equal documents, a scoped nested
+  change, member add/remove, scalar replace, root type mismatch, path escaping, array append/insert/
+  remove, round-trip application via `applyPatch` across a variety of documents, and non-mutation of
+  both inputs), confirmed they failed against the not-yet-implemented function, then implemented
+  `createPatch` until all 72 tests in the suite passed.
+
+## Follow-ups not done
+
+- No `move`/`copy` detection and no similarity matching for array elements that changed instead of
+  being added/removed outright (see dl-004's consequences). Out of scope for this request, which only
+  asked for a patch that omits unchanged parts, not a globally shortest one.
